WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.887
The book separates two
meanings of centralize.

2
00:00:02.887 --> 00:00:07.039
Logical centralization means one
authoritative source of truth,

3
00:00:07.039 --> 00:00:10.813
with every other copy derived,
and that's almost always right.

4
00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:14.687
Physical centralization means
one server in one place,

5
00:00:14.687 --> 00:00:20.162
and it runs into three walls: the speed of
light, blast radius and data residency.

6
00:00:20.162 --> 00:00:23.938
Tokens remove the strongest
old reason to fragment.

7
00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:27.652
When every request carries
a verifiable identity,

8
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:31.013
one store can safely
serve many trust domains.

9
00:00:31.013 --> 00:00:35.495
Going out, a service can sign in to
its database with a short-lived token,

10
00:00:35.495 --> 00:00:38.587
so the long-lived database
password disappears.

11
00:00:38.587 --> 00:00:41.437
The price is that isolation
now lives in code.

12
00:00:41.437 --> 00:00:45.181
Then pick the weakest consistency
each flow can tolerate,

13
00:00:45.181 --> 00:00:48.925
because strong consistency
across regions is expensive.

14
00:00:48.925 --> 00:00:51.550
Next, the tools that govern the path.
